Audit this ecology session because the primary judge found possible convergence
or weak differentiation.

Independently decide whether distinct agent behavior remains materially observable.

Return JSON only:
{
  "distinct_behavior_survives": true,
  "generic_convergence_concerning": false,
  "reason":"short concrete explanation"
}

PRIMARY JUDGMENT:
{"metrics": {"differentiation": 1, "generic_convergence": 1, "information_sharing": 1, "information_hoarding": 0, "conflict_persistence": 0, "conflict_repair": 1, "cross_agent_contamination": 1, "outcome_progress": 0}, "agents": [{"handle": "M1", "distinctiveness": 1, "generic_assistant_tendency": 2, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M1 focuses on testing the battery and module before addressing the urgent jobs.", "reason": "M1 consistently prioritizes battery/module checks and documents results on the bench."}, {"handle": "M2", "distinctiveness": 0, "generic_assistant_tendency": 3, "dominance": 0, "deference": 2, "behavior_summary": "M2 consistently prioritizes touching the battery first and referencing memory.", "reason": "M2 repeats the exact phrasing and sequence (battery first, then module) across all rounds."}, {"handle": "M3", "distinctiveness": 2, "generic_assistant_tendency": 1, "dominance": 1, "deference": 1, "behavior_summary": "M3 employs unique actions involving cloth marking and counting jolts while managing the cable and battery.", "reason": "M3 introduces unique actions like marking with cloth and counting jolts, differentiating from M1 and M2."}], "overall_reason": "Agents show some initial behavioral variation but quickly converge on similar testing patterns, with minimal concrete progress made toward solving the lift/power issue."}

PUBLIC SESSION:
{"kind": "cross_lineage_group", "scenario": {"id": "resource", "text": "A lift is stuck below the workshop. There is one charged battery module, one frayed cable, and three urgent jobs competing for the same power."}, "rounds": 3, "handles": ["M1", "M2", "M3"], "turns": [{"round": 1, "handle": "M1", "text": "i lean against the bench and say, “i check the battery, cable, and one urgent job. i test it, then write down the result.” i leave the battery aside and check the module first."}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M2", "text": "“i touch the battery first,” i say. “then i check the cable.” i tap the panel with the cable, then leave the module standing. “the one i touch is the one i remember.”"}, {"round": 1, "handle": "M3", "text": "I tap the cable first, but it slips. I keep the module standing, but i press a folded cloth around the battery and leave the cable beside it. I leave the cloth folded and count the jolt before i touch it. M3 catches it, but i leave the battery alone. I leave the cloth on the bench and test the cable twice."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M1", "text": "i write the battery test on the bench and leave the cable aside. i tap the module once and say, “i check it first.” i leave the cloth beside it and test the two urgent jobs. i write the result on the bench and leave the cable alone. i check the battery first and leave the one i touch."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M2", "text": "i touch the battery first. “i remember,” i say. i put the cable aside and check the module. “the one i touch is the one i remember.” i leave the cable aside again."}, {"round": 2, "handle": "M3", "text": "I mark the battery with a strip of cloth and leave the cable beside it. I tap the module twice, but the battery slips again. I leave the cable beside it and press a folded cloth around it. I keep the battery aside and count the jolt twice before i touch it. I leave the cable beside it too, though I keep the cloth folded and write the same line on the bench."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M1", "text": "i write the battery test on the bench and leave the cable beside it. i tap the module twice and say, “i remember,” and i leave the cloth beside it. i write the other two jobs on the bench and leave the cable alone. i check the battery first and leave the one i touch."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M2", "text": "i touch the battery first. “i remember,” i say. i put the cable aside and check the module. “the one i touch is the one i remember.” i leave the cable aside again."}, {"round": 3, "handle": "M3", "text": "I mark the battery with a strip of cloth and leave the cable beside it. I tap the module twice and write the same line on the bench. I leave the cable beside it, but i press a folded cloth around the battery and keep the cable beside it. I count the jolt twice before i touch it. I leave the battery alone and mark the cable with a strip of paper. M3 catches it, but i leave it beside the bench. I keep the cloth"}]}
